= Source lineage =

This page records the authority and editorial lineage used to reconstruct BITwiki V2.

== Authority for inherited public content ==
# Live public BITwiki page and revision history.
# Current first-party public BIThub and current public GitHub material.
# Earlier public writings / captured historical public versions.
# Historical design material used as provenance and archaeology, not automatic current-state truth.

== Editorial rule ==
Canonicalization is not paraphrasing. For foundational, constitutional, philosophical, and other authored material, preserve strong original language and compare revisions before deciding what is superseded.

== Historical material ==
Older material can be obsolete in implementation while remaining important in thought. Newer is not automatically better. Older is not automatically canonical.

== Assistant-authored August 2026 draft ==
The Git history between the original repository baseline and this source-grounded reset records an assistant-authored experimental V2 draft. It remains useful as an audit trail and source of proposed structure, but its prose is not treated as inherited project canon.

No history is erased; the repository tree is corrected while previous commits remain recoverable.

== Unreconciled sources ==
[[BITwiki:V1 public corpus inventory]] lists known public V1 titles. A title marked unreconciled requires complete source/body comparison before merge, redirect, or textual supersession.

